    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>\"Your blood remembers the higher spheres. Light hangs around you a little too long, and prayers sometimes answer themselves.\"</em></p>\n<p><strong>Sephirotic Physiology.</strong> You have resistance to sephirotic damage. Your blood runs a little bright under the right light; you do not technically age while on consecrated ground.</p>\n<p><strong>Sefirot Attunement (1/scene).</strong> At creation, pick one sephirah. Once per scene you can invoke its register before a roll: your next check that falls clearly within that sephirah's domain gains +1.</p>\n<p><strong>Holy Conduit.</strong> Manifestations, rituals, and other sephirotic-register effects that target you or pass through your space treat their caster's attribute as +1 for the duration of that effect. Works on allies and on you; never on qliphothic-register effects.</p>\n<p><strong>Light of Harmony.</strong> When you reach an explicit, spoken agreement with another creature, you and that creature each gain 1 temporary Integrity.</p>",
